WEBVTT

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.500
Karte 4 - Anorexia, The Two Dark Doctors

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.030
<i>The patient wants to live.</i>

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.470
<i>That is what the doctor</i>
<i>believes and strives to help...</i>

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.200
<i>to the best of his abilities.</i>

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.580
<i>If death comes, even after</i>
<i>every effort has been made...</i>

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:37.620
<i>we must accept that.</i>

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:42.980
<i>But at times, some patients</i>
<i>lose their will to fight...</i>

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.090
<i>and give in to despair.</i>

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.970
You're here at last...

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:02.630
Finally, I will be relieved of my suffering,
thanks to you.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.830
I'm only helping out a little bit.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.380
About your fee...

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.850
Please don't worry. Your son deposited the
amount into my account yesterday.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.520
Do you like Beethoven?

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:35.300
You're going to fall asleep listening
to music, just like always...

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:38.110
But this sleep is just a
little deeper than usual...

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:42.210
That's all it is...

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:07.740
Why hello, Doctor Black Jack.
Is the patient inside one of your patients?

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:12.110
Doctor Kiriko...
What are you doing here?

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:15.300
Who knows? We're both
professionals in the underworld.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.280
Let's spare each other the questions.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:33.560
Oh, that's right. Your patient just
passed away of natural causes.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.300
What?

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.880
How come? We agreed I'd
operate on him next week.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.850
I'm sorry, Dr. Black Jack.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:02.760
My father said he was tired...
that he'd lived long enough...

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:51.740
As my heart lay in pieces
from being shot

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:55.650
In the waves of people
who pass me by

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:59.640
I even forgot what kindness is

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:03.280
I slip from your hands

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:07.190
The night I disappeared
from that city

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.230
I held only my dreams

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.900
Never looking back

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:19.040
It twines around me so painfully

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.130
Stop this loneliness

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:30.110
As if you are going to erase
the sorrow of these skies

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:34.720
If fate should have us part

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:37.710
I will journey through it

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:42.460
And take you with might

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:46.560
The one of my memories

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.140
There you are.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.340
Michelle. Ten minutes before we shoot!

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:37.240
Let's get on the set while
the director's still in a good mood.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:46.580
You know...
You don't look so well, Michelle.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.690
Hi, I'm a reporter from <i>Evening Celebrity.</i>

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.700
We're in Studio 6.
You know where it is, right, Michelle?

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:54.960
Yes...

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.330
Stop following her around already!

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.270
Is something wrong with her?

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.470
She's healthy as she can be!

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:07.710
Oh really? I've heard she's fainted
on the set a couple of times.

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:13.410
Her current role is very demanding.
Perhaps she pushed herself too hard?

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:20.990
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:25.030
You're the purest and most
innocent existence in this world.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.130
Can you do this shot, Michelle?

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:30.190
Yes, Director! I can do it! I will!

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:33.800
On top of that,
people are still wondering...

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.560
why would such a
great director like Alex...

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:39.810
cast a second rate porno
actress like her as his lead.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:44.380
She's a wonderful actress.
She was just underrated until now.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.690
Did she bribe him or sleep
with him? Which one is it?

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:51.490
You son of a bitch!

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:06.600
Scene 85! It's the final scene!
Let's do it!

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:09.470
And... action!

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:48.470
Cut!

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:51.910
Michelle! Michelle!

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:53.940
Stop the camera! Stop!

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:56.050
Call an ambulance! Call the hospital!

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:00.950
I'm sorry, Alex... I'm sorry...

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:13.930
She is showing visible signs
of stress and malnutrition.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.200
She needs to get some rest.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:21.010
I see. Then we'll postpone
the shoot for a week.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:22.910
We'd be grateful.

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:25.240
Rest up and we'll shoot
the final scene.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:27.680
We're almost there, Michelle.

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:30.920
Thank you very much, Alex.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.980
It's going to be a great movie.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:35.790
I'm thinking about casting you
for my next movie too.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:38.360
Well, if you'll excuse us, Alex.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:39.900
Yes, I'll see you soon.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:45.530
You're pushing yourself too hard.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:48.040
I understand getting into your
part, but there's a limit!

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:52.300
You need to eat.
It's hard for you to stand, right?

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:48.900
'Morning, Michelle!

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:53.130
I've brought you a healthy,
balanced breakfast to cheer you up!

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:57.000
I had it made especially for you by
the head chef at Restaurant Cartier.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:00.500
Cheerio! Time to wake up!
Show me that beautiful smile!

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:03.340
Michelle, wake up!

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:06.410
It's your manager, Patrick!

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:07.740
Mich...

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:13.560
<i>I promise I will call.</i>
<i>Please don't try to find me.</i>

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:15.720
<i>Best wishes Patrick.</i>
<i>- Michelle.</i>

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:37.970
Sir, you have a phone call.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:40.780
Just how long a
vacation are you taking?

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:45.380
Have you forgotten that <i>I'm</i>
waiting for you at home?

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:49.320
I get it! You're not alone!
You're with someone, aren't you?

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:54.230
Put her on the phone!
I'll talk to her myself!

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:57.160
Put that cake-face
hussy on the phone!

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:01.360
I currently cannot get to the phone.
Please try your call later.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.070
Hey! You better not hang up!
Don't hang up!!

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:07.040
What is it? Is this urgent?

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:13.880
Hmph. It may not be urgent, but
they seemed like they were in a rush.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.310
Cahros Chabanon Village?

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:21.850
Yup. It's in the central,
mountainous area of France.

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:24.890
They're only offering $200,000.
It's really not that much.

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:32.600
<i>After seeing a patient in Switzerland,</i>
<i>I was taking a vacation in Arles...</i>

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:34.300
<i>only to be interrupted</i>
<i>with an assignment.</i>

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:38.630
<i>My vacations are always</i>
<i>cut short like this.</i>

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:41.340
<i>Next time I'll go swim to</i>
<i>the bottom of the sea...</i>

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:43.040
<i>so I can't be reachable by phone.</i>

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:58.330
I'm Armand Rochass.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:03.060
Dr. Black Jack. I can't believe you've come.
It's like a dream come true.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:07.800
I'm only a country doctor,
but being in the medical field...

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:10.930
I've heard quite a bit about you.

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:13.370
Hey! Bring us your best bottle of wine!

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:15.040
Please...

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:30.290
I was told the patient is anorexic,
but the cause is unknown.

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:33.600
Yes. Please see for yourself.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:37.790
Other than fluids, the poor girl hasn't
been able to keep anything down...

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:39.840
for twenty days now. Not even a liquid diet.

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:43.330
She was such a beautiful girl.
I feel so sorry for her.

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:47.940
The patient is my niece.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:53.840
She came to me for help, but I'm afraid
I haven't been able to do anything for her.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.410
I normally only deal with cows and horses.

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:01.090
When I told my niece that, she said...

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:04.160
"I have two hundred thousand dollars."

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:07.890
"Please get Dr. Black Jack to look at me.
I hear he's the best doctor in the world."

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:11.670
I've brought him, Michelle.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:17.610
Please don't turn on the light just yet...

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:19.970
Michelle...

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:26.050
I have a favor to ask Dr. Black Jack
before he sees me in the light.

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:33.220
To be honest, I have only a hundred
and twenty thousand dollars saved up.

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:37.750
The remaining eighty thousand
is my pay for my current movie.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:42.060
I won't be paid unless
the movie is finished.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:46.930
Until I recover from my illness,
we won't be able to shoot the last scene.

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:50.270
In the event I'm not able to be cured...

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.580
will you forgive me that I can only pay
you a hundred and twenty thousand?

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:59.410
My fee is two hundred thousand.

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:04.920
After a full recovery you will pay
the remaining eighty thousand. Okay?

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:07.930
Until then, your only concern
is to get well, understand?

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:13.660
Come, lie down.
I want to start the examination.

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:19.270
I want to act.
I want to act in the movie!

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:23.570
To be an actress...
I want to be a real actress!

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:36.120
The patient was Michelle Rochass, age 32.

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:41.350
Her stage name is Michelle Petit,
but I had never heard of her.

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:49.230
I can't forget about you!

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:51.470
No!

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.040
Okay, you can stop.

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:20.830
I want the long shot from Camera B
inserted after Michelle's close up.

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:22.030
You got it, sir.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:24.760
A woman's charm is in her sinful beauty.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:26.500
Yes.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:31.760
Alex!

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:41.120
I'll be honest... lt's been ten days,
but I haven't heard anything.

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:46.790
She only has one scene left!
Why she'd disappear like this is beyond me.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.180
I negotiated with the studio today.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:53.590
I convinced them to give me
another month to finish the shoot.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:55.830
Alex.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.340
So I want you to find her no matter what.

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:05.810
Why are you so insistent on Michelle?

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:09.210
Come on. It's part of being a director.

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:39.570
I traveled to Paris when I was 17,
to become an actress.

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:45.250
I worked part-time while I went to
the Theatre Academy. I studied so hard.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:47.780
I graduated...

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:52.420
But my first job was
posing nude for a photogravure.

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:56.130
I was desperate for money,
so I accepted the job, but...

00:16:57.760 --> 00:17:00.230
I think that's where I went wrong.

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.300
The next movie was a porn film.

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:07.600
Then the next, and the next...
They were all porn.

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:11.300
When did you start
to lose your appetite?

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:16.810
When I finally landed this part,
I tried to lose ten pounds.

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:21.580
The woman I was playing was
several years younger than me.

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:23.720
To look more convincing,
I wanted to lose ten pounds.

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:26.620
It was a simple diet
where I skipped lunch.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:31.130
I reached my target
weight and ended my diet...

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.320
but then I started to lose
the urge to eat breakfast...

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.460
then dinner...

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:41.630
Finally, my body became unable
to hold down anything except liquids.

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:53.380
<i>I gave the patient hormones</i>
<i>and nutrients via IV.</i>

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:57.420
<i>The first thing was to stop</i>
<i>the progression of malnutrition.</i>

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:03.330
<i>But it would only be enough to cover</i>
<i>forty percent of her basic metabolism.</i>

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:06.860
<i>If her condition persists,</i>
<i>she will die of starvation.</i>

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:10.160
Did she fall asleep?

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:15.330
Yes. I think she's very much comforted
by the fact that you're here.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:21.340
Anorexia is often diagnosed
as a mental illness...

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:25.010
but occasionally it can be triggered
by a tumor in the digestive tract...

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:29.880
or a hormonal imbalance brought on by a
problem in the body's endocrine system.

00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:32.260
Is that so?

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:35.090
In the case of a problem
in the endocrine system...

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:38.260
appetite and nutritional
intake are strongly affected.

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:40.690
I see...

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.720
I'd like to perform a thorough examination...

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:46.430
at a facility with the necessary
equipment. Can you arrange that?

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:48.200
Forgive me for saying this,
but your office isn't...

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:52.730
No, I totally understand what you're
saying. Please leave it to me.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:56.240
Catina...

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:58.280
Catina!

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:03.080
Catina! Where are you?

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:14.000
Catina!

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:25.140
I hate you, Catina!

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:28.310
Sorry, Michelle! I'm sorry.

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:29.640
Hmph!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:32.280
Well, time for another funeral!

00:19:33.890 --> 00:19:36.720
You'll be the relative and
I'll be the reverend.

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:37.950
OK!

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:46.000
We pray this day for the soul of our
lost friend, whose death teaches us...

00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:50.000
the value of our own precious lives.
And we ask when our own time has come...

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:53.400
we be reunited in Heaven with thee...

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:58.900
Michelle, what do you think
I'll be when I grow up?

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:00.480
I don't know.

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:03.010
How could you not? A writer!

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:05.610
I want to become a world-
renowned writer like Sagan!

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:08.170
You think I'm talented, right?

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:11.920
Yeah, you'll be a writer.
You know everything.

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:15.660
How about you, Michelle?
What do you want to be?

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.260
Tell me!

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:19.990
An actress.

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:22.430
A superstar!

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:25.770
I want to be an amazing actress
that everyone will fall in love with!

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:32.370
Well, that's what I hope.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.980
You'll grow up to be
beautiful, Michelle!

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:38.910
You'll be much more beautiful
when you grow up!

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:01.440
A little slower.

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:03.800
I want to get a good look at the esophagus,
all the way to the cardia.

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:05.310
Yes, sir.

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:18.280
<i>We preformed a thorough examination</i>
<i>at a public hospital where...</i>

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:21.380
<i>Armand's old friend from school</i>
<i>serves as the senior medical staff.</i>

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:25.130
<i>Fortunately, there was a ten hour opening...</i>

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:27.460
<i>in the examination room with</i>
<i>the latest medical equipment.</i>

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:29.330
<i>Within that time frame...</i>

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:33.600
<i>I had to consider every possibility</i>
<i>and collect as much data as possible.</i>

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:41.440
<i>We continuously monitored Michelle's</i>
<i>decrease in strength and...</i>

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:43.740
<i>continued the invasive exams.</i>

00:21:55.190 --> 00:21:59.320
<i>The patient was very tolerant and</i>
<i>completed every exam necessary.</i>

00:22:00.200 --> 00:22:04.600
<i>It was positive proof this patient</i>
<i>had the desire to live.</i>

00:22:13.210 --> 00:22:15.740
I think it'd be wise to
keep your window closed.

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:19.310
No, I like it. It feels so refreshing...

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:25.680
Uncle... I'd like to go visit Catina's grave.

00:22:26.090 --> 00:22:29.990
We can't get there from this highway.
We'd have to go all the way around.

00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:34.260
We'll go next time, Michelle.

00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:41.930
Catina was Michelle's childhood friend.

00:22:42.970 --> 00:22:46.030
Michelle was born and raised
in a village called Anjou.

00:22:46.110 --> 00:22:49.880
Her parents divorced when she was
twelve. A lot of things happened...

00:22:49.950 --> 00:22:52.540
and I became her guardian.

00:22:56.120 --> 00:22:59.110
Catina was two years
older than Michelle...

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:02.130
and used to play with Michelle a lot.

00:23:03.090 --> 00:23:07.220
I was to be an actress...
Catina was going to be a writer.

00:23:08.300 --> 00:23:12.830
Catina died of an illness a year later,
after Michelle came to live with me.

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:21.270
I heard she died of pneumonia.

00:23:26.780 --> 00:23:29.950
<i>That night I began analyzing the</i>
<i>data from the examinations.</i>

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:34.650
<i>A decrease in her health from</i>
<i>malnutrition would increase...</i>

00:23:34.730 --> 00:23:37.390
<i>the possibilities of</i>
<i>various complications.</i>

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:42.000
<i>There are the possibilities of</i>
<i>increased infection rate,</i>

00:23:42.070 --> 00:23:45.730
<i>abnormalities in her cardiopulmonary</i>
<i>system, and even septic fever.</i>

00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:48.900
<i>I had no time to waste in attempting</i>
<i>to isolate the cause of her illness.</i>

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:53.900
<i>I found no sign of abnormality</i>
<i>in her digestive tract...</i>

00:23:54.350 --> 00:23:56.510
<i>nor did I find anything wrong</i>
<i>with her endocrine system.</i>

00:23:58.280 --> 00:24:01.680
<i>Activity in her adrenal gland</i>
<i>had slightly decreased...</i>

00:24:02.290 --> 00:24:05.380
<i>but I can't imagine how this could</i>
<i>translate into loss of weight.</i>

00:24:11.730 --> 00:24:14.720
<i>Lack of appetite could be commonly</i>
<i>caused by drugs or medication but...</i>

00:24:15.530 --> 00:24:19.440
<i>I could find no sign of</i>
<i>either in the test results.</i>

00:24:20.570 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>All blood tests came back negative.</i>

00:24:31.120 --> 00:24:32.550
<i>If that's the case...</i>

00:24:33.650 --> 00:24:35.980
<i>could there be something wrong</i>
<i>with the limbic system...</i>

00:24:36.050 --> 00:24:37.580
<i>of the central nervous system?</i>

00:24:39.960 --> 00:24:42.890
<i>It can't be. I can't find anything unusual</i>
<i>in her CT scan of her brain...</i>

00:24:42.960 --> 00:24:44.890
<i>and electroencephalogram.</i>

00:24:52.170 --> 00:24:54.690
I want freshly baked
bread and marmalade...

00:24:56.910 --> 00:24:59.430
scrambled eggs too.

00:25:00.440 --> 00:25:01.640
Michelle.

00:25:02.450 --> 00:25:04.210
I'm going to try it once more...

00:25:04.650 --> 00:25:08.880
I can't keep being such a
burden on you and Dr. Black Jack.

00:25:28.570 --> 00:25:30.170
It looks wonderful...

00:26:13.750 --> 00:26:15.150
Welcome.

00:26:20.460 --> 00:26:21.930
Hello! Hello!

00:26:21.990 --> 00:26:27.590
It's the greatest honor to meet the lead
actress' manager and director at once.

00:26:28.270 --> 00:26:30.670
You better be right about this!

00:26:32.240 --> 00:26:35.500
Well, if you don't want to shelve
your almost completed film...

00:26:35.570 --> 00:26:38.080
you might want to listen
to what I have to tell you.

00:26:38.080 --> 00:26:40.700
Is it true you know where she is?

00:26:42.480 --> 00:26:45.040
Well... about a week ago...

00:26:46.680 --> 00:26:50.780
She apparently underwent a thorough
physical exam at a certain hospital...

00:26:50.860 --> 00:26:54.990
as Michelle Rochass, her real
name, instead of Michelle Petit.

00:26:57.530 --> 00:27:00.090
If you want to know more,
you'll have to pay for it.

00:27:00.160 --> 00:27:06.760
Well, you know, I spent a lot of money
to get this information, so...

00:27:06.970 --> 00:27:08.370
Fine.

00:27:18.220 --> 00:27:22.410
Hey, Catina... it's so bizarre...

00:27:24.560 --> 00:27:28.220
Look, these are my favorite rings...

00:27:29.330 --> 00:27:33.020
They used to fit my fingers so perfectly.
They were so beautiful...

00:27:35.200 --> 00:27:39.930
But look... When I do this...

00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:12.990
Michelle... What's wrong?

00:28:13.640 --> 00:28:17.160
I want to see... I want to see Catina!

00:28:18.410 --> 00:28:19.740
Michelle...

00:28:19.810 --> 00:28:21.140
I want to see her!

00:28:22.680 --> 00:28:25.340
Michelle!
What's happened to your face?

00:28:46.740 --> 00:28:48.300
Michelle!

00:28:51.180 --> 00:28:52.640
Michelle!

00:28:59.580 --> 00:29:02.280
Michelle, open this door!
Open this door!

00:29:08.630 --> 00:29:11.620
Get back in bed! Don't do this!

00:29:12.960 --> 00:29:14.260
Please move!

00:29:22.340 --> 00:29:23.600
Are you all right?

00:29:24.410 --> 00:29:26.310
Erythema on her forehead...

00:29:26.840 --> 00:29:28.970
I think I've seen it somewhere before...

00:29:38.020 --> 00:29:41.750
She probably is headed towards Anjou
where she was born and raised.

00:29:43.560 --> 00:29:45.790
I'll go ask the pastor if
we could borrow his car.

00:30:35.080 --> 00:30:38.710
How did you let yourself
get this malnourished? Eat this.

00:30:41.820 --> 00:30:45.050
I administered glucose to supply
you with some nutrients.

00:30:47.190 --> 00:30:48.680
You should have some.

00:30:49.290 --> 00:30:51.660
Are you a doctor?

00:30:52.960 --> 00:30:56.190
I guess I was... a long time ago...

00:30:56.870 --> 00:30:59.800
But these days I'm a full-time drifter.

00:31:01.410 --> 00:31:04.000
Although I still practice by
special request sometimes.

00:31:07.810 --> 00:31:09.800
Is this Beethoven?

00:31:11.120 --> 00:31:12.550
I composed it myself.

00:31:14.390 --> 00:31:15.750
So you're a musician.

00:31:16.020 --> 00:31:18.280
A musician. That's great.

00:31:26.760 --> 00:31:31.430
Your car is totaled. Even if you
get it towed, it's not salvageable.

00:31:33.100 --> 00:31:34.430
It's a lovely song.

00:31:35.410 --> 00:31:38.970
I'll bring you home. I'm not
abandoning a seriously ill person.

00:31:39.940 --> 00:31:41.940
I'd much rather die...

00:31:58.060 --> 00:32:00.050
Hey!

00:32:02.800 --> 00:32:04.830
Hey! Sir!

00:32:20.880 --> 00:32:23.980
I've seen those erythema
somewhere before.

00:32:28.390 --> 00:32:31.420
Leave. You're going to
interfere with my work.

00:32:33.560 --> 00:32:34.860
Are you leaving?

00:32:35.030 --> 00:32:36.360
Thanks for your hospitality.

00:32:36.430 --> 00:32:39.060
Won't you stay for dinner?
I want to repay you.

00:32:44.710 --> 00:32:46.570
Can you at least tell me your name?

00:32:48.110 --> 00:32:49.370
Mozart.

00:32:51.120 --> 00:32:53.740
Why don't we leave it at that?
Take care.

00:33:01.230 --> 00:33:03.220
<i>Seven new erythema.</i>

00:33:03.960 --> 00:33:06.660
<i>They're appearing in proportion</i>
<i>to her increasing emaciation.</i>

00:33:08.630 --> 00:33:11.290
<i>I know I've seen them before...</i>
<i>But where?</i>

00:33:12.300 --> 00:33:13.600
Damn it!

00:33:22.780 --> 00:33:24.710
Doctor, I've prepared dinner.

00:33:25.420 --> 00:33:26.970
Thank you.

00:33:34.990 --> 00:33:37.120
I want to take a shower.

00:34:05.960 --> 00:34:09.150
Catina... I can't anymore...

00:34:21.710 --> 00:34:25.230
No! Don't! Noooo!

00:34:32.680 --> 00:34:34.240
Found it.

00:34:34.320 --> 00:34:38.690
Armand Rochass, Doctor of Internal
Medicine and Pediatrics.

00:34:43.190 --> 00:34:45.020
No visitors allowed!?

00:34:45.400 --> 00:34:49.460
Oh, come on...
We came all the way from Paris.

00:34:50.070 --> 00:34:55.440
Please, let us see her.
Her life as an actress is at stake!

00:34:56.170 --> 00:34:59.440
To hell with that!
My niece's life is at stake!

00:35:07.750 --> 00:35:09.720
There's something I'd like to ask you.

00:35:10.220 --> 00:35:12.350
Let's go, Alex!

00:35:12.490 --> 00:35:17.120
By any chance, are there red skin sores
appearing all over Michelle's body?

00:35:19.400 --> 00:35:21.090
I suspected that was the case.

00:35:21.570 --> 00:35:24.130
How do you know about them?

00:35:24.330 --> 00:35:26.170
Alex!

00:35:26.800 --> 00:35:28.740
Go back to the hotel without me.

00:35:30.240 --> 00:35:31.670
All righty then.

00:35:43.720 --> 00:35:48.590
My younger sister Catina was covered in
these exact skin sores before she died.

00:35:50.690 --> 00:35:54.290
I work as a movie director
under the name Alex Ray...

00:35:54.730 --> 00:35:58.790
but my real name is Nicholas
Aleco, Catina Aleco's older brother.

00:36:00.570 --> 00:36:04.530
I'm sure Michelle doesn't know
that I'm Catina's brother.

00:36:05.640 --> 00:36:09.170
My parents sent me to a boarding
school in Paris after elementary school.

00:36:09.910 --> 00:36:12.940
But I was rather familiar
with Michelle's name.

00:36:13.720 --> 00:36:18.480
She wrote of nothing but
Michelle in the letters she sent me.

00:36:20.120 --> 00:36:26.120
We chose the leading actress
through an audition, but what a surprise.

00:36:26.700 --> 00:36:31.000
I later found out that Michelle Petite's
real name was Michelle Rochass.

00:36:31.070 --> 00:36:34.300
I was told your sister died of pneumonia.

00:36:35.210 --> 00:36:38.040
We asked the doctor
to change her charts...

00:36:38.480 --> 00:36:41.470
It was such a perplexing
and heartbreaking death...

00:36:44.510 --> 00:36:48.710
She became unable to eat...
Withered away like a dying tree...

00:36:48.790 --> 00:36:54.050
In the end, her body was covered
in red skin sores when she passed away.

00:36:57.730 --> 00:37:02.030
When I heard Michelle was
suspected of malnutrition...

00:37:02.030 --> 00:37:05.060
Catina's illness crossed my mind
and I became very worried.

00:37:17.750 --> 00:37:20.910
These red markings, this "Erythema"...

00:37:21.520 --> 00:37:23.010
existed eighteen years ago.

00:37:24.020 --> 00:37:26.250
There was only one solid
link between Michelle and Catina.

00:37:28.060 --> 00:37:29.460
The village of Anjou.

00:37:31.460 --> 00:37:36.300
Her blood pressure is going down.
Please add aminophylline to her IV.

00:37:36.570 --> 00:37:38.930
If it falls below 60, please increase it.

00:37:39.470 --> 00:37:40.630
Yes, sir.

00:37:44.810 --> 00:37:46.170
Dr. Black Jack!

00:37:46.940 --> 00:37:48.270
I'll be back before dawn.

00:38:22.180 --> 00:38:23.810
I've brought this for you.

00:38:24.280 --> 00:38:26.720
It's about chemical
and biological weapons...

00:38:26.780 --> 00:38:29.050
that were banned after World War I.

00:38:29.490 --> 00:38:33.980
Published in 1921, by the
International Pathological Association.

00:38:34.660 --> 00:38:36.420
I am an expert in toxicology,

00:38:36.490 --> 00:38:38.460
but it took me a while to remember...

00:38:38.530 --> 00:38:40.390
because the records are so old.

00:38:41.100 --> 00:38:43.120
Take a look at page 238.

00:38:55.350 --> 00:38:59.610
<i>The bacteria can only survive inside</i>
<i>a particular kind of Echinococcus.</i>

00:39:00.150 --> 00:39:02.120
<i>"This disease-carrying</i>
<i>Echinococcus will be engineered...</i>

00:39:02.190 --> 00:39:03.850
<i>to act as an incredibly toxic weapon. "</i>

00:39:05.190 --> 00:39:06.210
This can't be!

00:39:06.290 --> 00:39:09.220
I haven't found any traces of
such a parasite in Michelle!

00:39:09.290 --> 00:39:12.920
I'd like to present you
another interesting fact.

00:39:13.630 --> 00:39:15.890
Near the village of Anjou...
around here...

00:39:15.970 --> 00:39:18.100
are the ruins of the military's
explosives warehouse.

00:39:18.100 --> 00:39:20.470
But it doesn't store explosives.

00:39:20.800 --> 00:39:24.570
Rather, it's a permanent dumping
ground for biological weapons.

00:39:52.770 --> 00:39:54.400
Would you like to play
a game of chess?

00:39:54.470 --> 00:39:56.270
- No, thank you.
- Some wine, then?

00:40:09.520 --> 00:40:11.580
I'm going away, so
I thought I'd stop by...

00:40:13.860 --> 00:40:15.350
How beautiful!

00:40:16.930 --> 00:40:20.160
I envy you. I want to go too...
To a place far away...

00:40:26.070 --> 00:40:27.930
I know this is a strange question, but...

00:40:29.910 --> 00:40:34.170
Is it true there's a professional
doctor who euthanizes his patients?

00:40:36.780 --> 00:40:39.010
Someone told me about him before...

00:40:40.480 --> 00:40:43.320
He's a professional who specializes
in euthanasia and will come...

00:40:43.390 --> 00:40:46.010
wherever, whenever the patient wishes
and gives them a peaceful death...

00:40:46.090 --> 00:40:47.580
as long as you pay his fee.

00:40:48.160 --> 00:40:52.060
His name is... Doctor... Doctor...

00:40:56.630 --> 00:41:00.570
If you know who he is, please tell me.
I want to get in contact with him.

00:41:01.070 --> 00:41:02.770
I thought he charges a fee?

00:41:04.240 --> 00:41:08.080
That's right...
I'm absolutely penniless now...

00:41:08.310 --> 00:41:10.440
Right? Then, that's not an option.

00:41:40.210 --> 00:41:44.170
<i>It was obvious this was the village</i>
<i>children's secret playground.</i>

00:41:55.190 --> 00:41:58.490
<i>The countless corpses of small animals</i>
<i>were a testament that the bacteria...</i>

00:41:58.930 --> 00:42:02.520
<i>that was meant to be permanently buried</i>
<i>over ten meters underground...</i>

00:42:03.030 --> 00:42:06.260
<i>had risen to the surface</i>
<i>and continued to survive.</i>

00:42:09.040 --> 00:42:12.480
<i>This was, no doubt, the place where</i>
<i>Catina and Michelle were infected.</i>

00:43:09.700 --> 00:43:13.470
Doctor, I suggest you
get some rest tonight.

00:43:15.310 --> 00:43:16.930
Oh, nothing.

00:43:18.940 --> 00:43:20.940
Would it be possible for you
to make some coffee?

00:43:20.940 --> 00:43:22.210
Yes, right away.

00:43:36.360 --> 00:43:38.490
Are you well enough to answer
some questions, Michelle?

00:43:39.000 --> 00:43:40.020
Yes.

00:43:40.530 --> 00:43:42.660
Do you know about the old
explosives warehouse near Anjou?

00:43:43.230 --> 00:43:44.060
Of course.

00:43:44.130 --> 00:43:45.500
Have you been there recently?

00:43:45.970 --> 00:43:49.170
Yes, when I got the part for this movie...

00:43:49.640 --> 00:43:53.940
I went to Catina's grave to tell her about it.
I stopped by before I went home.

00:43:54.410 --> 00:43:55.740
For old times sake...

00:43:55.810 --> 00:43:57.780
Did anything unusual happen?

00:43:58.150 --> 00:44:04.280
Nothing really. Except, I was bitten by a rat...
It was only a little scratch though.

00:44:04.990 --> 00:44:06.250
A rat?

00:44:06.320 --> 00:44:07.190
Yes.

00:44:07.260 --> 00:44:08.420
Are you sure?

00:44:08.590 --> 00:44:09.320
Positive.

00:44:11.430 --> 00:44:14.330
Then I want to perform an
operation on you immediately.

00:44:16.800 --> 00:44:18.700
Trust me just once more.

00:44:27.980 --> 00:44:30.910
Check out of the hotel and get over
here immediately! He's operating!

00:44:30.980 --> 00:44:32.380
Michelle is going into surgery!

00:44:46.360 --> 00:44:48.100
We will be performing a
frontal cranial surgery.

00:44:48.100 --> 00:44:49.190
Yes, Doctor.

00:44:50.100 --> 00:44:51.590
<i>The answer was obvious.</i>

00:44:54.500 --> 00:44:56.670
<i>The biologically engineered</i>
<i>parasitic Echinococcus was nesting...</i>

00:44:56.740 --> 00:44:59.400
<i>in the appetitive central nervous</i>
<i>system in her limbic system.</i>

00:45:00.880 --> 00:45:03.780
<i>Normally a parasite would be</i>
<i>unable to enter the brain area,</i>

00:45:04.110 --> 00:45:07.080
<i>but it was probably developed</i>
<i>as a biological weapon...</i>

00:45:07.150 --> 00:45:10.050
<i>that could easily pass through</i>
<i>the blood-brain barrier.</i>

00:45:11.890 --> 00:45:15.260
<i>If I could find the parasite and remove it,</i>
<i>it should solve everything.</i>

00:45:18.030 --> 00:45:20.000
<i>But this wasn't going to</i>
<i>be as easy as it sounded.</i>

00:45:20.800 --> 00:45:22.660
<i>The tomogram of the brain we took...</i>

00:45:22.730 --> 00:45:25.290
<i>using the most modern equipment</i>
<i>at the public hospital...</i>

00:45:25.370 --> 00:45:28.860
<i>showed absolutely no sign of it.</i>

00:45:31.010 --> 00:45:34.410
<i>I was quite perplexed how the</i>
<i>parasite could be so invisible.</i>

00:45:34.810 --> 00:45:37.870
<i>The dead rat's corpse</i>
<i>solved that mystery.</i>

00:45:40.720 --> 00:45:44.050
<i>After opening the rat's brain,</i>
<i>all my questions were answered.</i>

00:45:45.920 --> 00:45:48.190
I'm going to make an incision
in the clavius arachnoid.

00:45:49.030 --> 00:45:49.960
Yes, sir.

00:45:50.030 --> 00:45:51.520
- Forceps.
- Forceps.

00:45:54.930 --> 00:45:57.060
All right. I've reached
the Chiasma Optimum.

00:45:57.370 --> 00:45:59.460
It's here! It has to be here.

00:46:02.610 --> 00:46:04.100
Yes! This is it!

00:46:04.940 --> 00:46:07.710
No, that's the nerve tissue!
It's not a parasite!

00:46:19.360 --> 00:46:20.720
It mimics its surroundings.

00:46:20.920 --> 00:46:24.960
The parasite mimics its physical
form to match exactly to its host.

00:46:24.960 --> 00:46:28.950
That's why we couldn't tell
them apart in the tomogram.

00:46:29.600 --> 00:46:32.000
I found the same exact
thing inside the rat's brain.

00:46:34.170 --> 00:46:37.630
This is beyond me...
I can't believe such a thing could exist.

00:46:42.080 --> 00:46:43.070
Pulse?

00:46:43.150 --> 00:46:44.580
Slow, but steady.

00:46:45.520 --> 00:46:47.040
Then, let's proceed with the sutures.

00:46:47.120 --> 00:46:48.480
Yes, doctor!

00:47:20.220 --> 00:47:21.510
Good... Good...

00:47:23.590 --> 00:47:25.880
Michelle Petit is so great!

00:47:26.060 --> 00:47:29.290
What? You're the one who wrote
all those tabloid articles on her!

00:47:29.290 --> 00:47:32.330
Work is work!
Aaa... She's so hot...

00:47:32.330 --> 00:47:33.350
Stop staring at her!

00:47:40.100 --> 00:47:42.830
The two are finally going to be together...

00:48:01.020 --> 00:48:04.960
What am I gonna do with you?
This always ends up happening.

00:48:19.840 --> 00:48:25.880
Many times I've asked the moon,
in search of an answer

00:48:25.880 --> 00:48:30.880
And I melt into the darkness

00:48:32.090 --> 00:48:39.960
Time flows in my heart, gone astray

00:48:44.400 --> 00:48:50.400
Today I look up at the sky
and it was as quiet as ever

00:48:50.770 --> 00:48:55.300
It surrounded itself around me again

00:48:56.550 --> 00:48:59.880
But it won't stop

00:48:59.880 --> 00:49:04.180
My burning heart wavers violently

00:49:08.590 --> 00:49:13.590
Even though I may get hurt

00:49:14.800 --> 00:49:20.970
I cannot utter lies, though...

00:49:20.970 --> 00:49:27.510
My tears have sunken
deep in my heart

00:49:27.510 --> 00:49:33.520
I gaze into a certain tomorrow

00:49:33.520 --> 00:49:44.390
To tell you how I feel

00:49:46.630 --> 00:49:52.100
The entangled dreams
have become too heavy

00:49:52.100 --> 00:49:57.940
They trickle away at
the cracks of my fingers

00:49:57.940 --> 00:50:09.150
Forever will remain as
something everlasting

00:50:11.290 --> 00:50:16.590
But I will soon start to walk again

00:50:16.590 --> 00:50:24.800
In order to not forget those days

00:50:25.540 --> 00:50:29.100
Subtitle Translation - Mayumi Kobayashi
DVD Subtitles - Justin Sevakis
